WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.095
Stage seventeen: before and after.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:12.923
Eight weeks planned up to the Trail des Crêtes: the form curve carries on as a dotted line, all the way to race day.

3
00:00:13.023 --> 00:00:21.188
Forecast form: plus twenty-six. Peak fatigue in the week of November second. An estimate from the plan, never a measurement.

4
00:00:22.038 --> 00:00:27.728
What if the taper lasted only one week? The variant is compared with the current plan.

5
00:00:27.828 --> 00:00:35.267
Six points of form lost on race day, eleven more of fatigue: two quiet weeks are justified, with numbers.

6
00:00:36.117 --> 00:00:46.308
Next year, the Ultra des Crêtes climbs to two thousand four hundred and fifty metres. Above fifteen hundred, each section slows with its altitude.

7
00:00:46.408 --> 00:00:54.424
Seventeen more minutes, for an athlete assumed not acclimatised; two weeks at altitude win back half of it, never all.

8
00:00:55.274 --> 00:01:04.271
Looking back, every coach decision has an aftermath: HRV, resting heart rate and readiness, three days before, three days after.

9
00:01:04.371 --> 00:01:12.727
Six lightened sessions assessed, five followed by an improvement. The only advice turned down was followed by a decline.

10
00:01:13.577 --> 00:01:21.550
Correlation, not causation: sleep, weather or chance play their part too. One case is not a trend; it takes five.

11
00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:27.724
And this review never relaxes a guardrail, a medical decision or a red verdict.

12
00:01:28.574 --> 00:01:36.141
After a race, the debrief compares plan and reality, segment by segment, and assigns the gap to each factor.

13
00:01:36.241 --> 00:01:45.963
At the Lucioles, the night cost twelve percent, against five planned. The coach proposes eight: pulled towards the default while evidence is scarce.

14
00:01:46.813 --> 00:01:56.428
Nothing is written without an explicit yes. From then on, every race plan reads these personal coefficients, and the next debrief refines them.

15
00:01:57.278 --> 00:02:03.501
Three documentation pages: load forecast, decision effects, the course strategist.

16
00:02:06.051 --> 00:02:10.290
To go further: the “/why” page of the documentation.
